## Fluxbot array data

This project processes the raw CO2 data collected from 55 fluxbots deployed across Gros Morne National Park in summer 2024: converting raw data into flux estimates, and subsequent analyses across the interacting environmental variables the deployment locations represented.

## Load packages

```{r}
library(dplyr)
library(tidyr)
library(here)
library(purrr)
library(stringr)
library(openxlsx)
library(readr)
```

## Converting raw data to flux estimates

Upload data: first use a custom function (xlsx_to_list.R) to read in the xlsx data files (one for each data stream: co2, pressure, temperature, and humidity) as a list, with each entry in the list corresponding to a fluxbot.

```{r}
#| echo: false
 
# function to import a single xlsx file with each tab as a separate df in a list of dfs with the name of the tab as the df name
read_excel_allsheets <- function(filename, tibble = FALSE) {
  # I prefer straight data.frames
  # but if you like tidyverse tibbles (the default with read_excel)
  # then just pass tibble = TRUE
  sheets <- readxl::excel_sheets(filename)
  x <- lapply(sheets, function(X) readxl::read_excel(filename, sheet = X))
  if(!tibble) x <- lapply(x, as.data.frame)
  names(x) <- sheets
  x
}

